 >
-> - **0.29.38** — [Keryx Desktop Review v2](keryx-desktop-review-v2/README.md). Draft requirements, nothing implemented. Splits the Pull requests board into a GitHub-only view of pull requests and issues and a separate Reviews entity (one review per pull request and reviewer, with rounds), defines what a review does when the pull request head moves, adds "Open in session" binding for pull requests and issues, and plans one review registry for Desktop and agent sessions.
+> - **0.29.38** — [Keryx Desktop Review v2](keryx-desktop-review-v2/README.md). Draft requirements; stage 0 (board fixes without a model change) is implemented in Flow 516, stages 1-4 are not. Splits the Pull requests board into a GitHub-only view of pull requests and issues and a separate Reviews entity (one review per pull request and reviewer, with rounds), defines what a review does when the pull request head moves, adds "Open in session" binding for pull requests and issues, and plans one review registry for Desktop and agent sessions.
 >
 > - [Desktop Review v1 implementation](keryx-desktop-review/live-acceptance.md) — the project board, manual review, local watcher and automatic rules are implemented. The acceptance record identifies the live macOS and GitHub scenarios, controlled events and remaining field checks.
 >
 > - **0.29.37** — [Keryx Desktop Telegram](keryx-desktop-telegram/README.md). Spec ready for local service setup and management from Integrations, QR or manual bot pairing, token replacement and explicit sharing of a live Desktop ACP session with Telegram. Scope includes revision-checked bot changes, poller readiness and recovery, turn arbitration, delegated approvals, and live-bot acceptance. Desktop runtime implementation is planned.
 >
 > - **0.29.36** — [OpenSpec in Keryx Metaproject](keryx-metaproject-openspec/README.md). Spec ready for owner review. Plans a local source alongside Graph and Wiki, with specs, active changes, archive, search and evidence-backed links. Draft Flow intake is a later increment. Runtime planned.
 >
 > - **0.29.35** — [Keryx Desktop: рабочие панели и внимание](keryx-desktop-workspace-panels/README.md) и [Готовность worktree](keryx-worktree-readiness/README.md). Draft requirements: attention tracked in Rust across all project views and windows (notifications, Dock badge, a Needs attention group), Changes and Files side tabs with path-and-line comments and `@path`, a context meter with compact, native image input once keryx accepts images (built on open PRs #1254 and #1256 and flow 493); worktree preparation (env files, copy-on-write dependencies, ports, local index rebuild), the worktree root and index for agents, `promote` of worktree findings to the user scope, a merge-conflict preview, and a report-only test baseline and flaky retry. Nothing implemented.
 >
 > - **0.29.34** — [Keryx Desktop Review v1](keryx-desktop-review/README.md). Draft requirements and delivery plan for the project PR board, manual review runs, a local watcher, and rule-based dispatch through review-orchestrator. Implementation planned.
 >
 > - **0.29.33**: [Keryx Desktop Client](keryx-desktop-client/README.md) — **M1 implemented on `feat/desktop-client`, owner acceptance pending**. macOS Tauri v2 client over `keryx acp --profile shell` (shell roster, ask/trust/auto modes, plan/usage updates, `_keryx/*` extensions), bundled keryx sidecar, local `.dmg`; shell parity in three milestones. Shares one Tauri app with Keryx Desktop App (D-08, awaiting owner confirmation).
 >
 > - **0.29.32**: [Keryx Desktop App](keryx-desktop-app/README.md) — **draft, nothing implemented; no Flow, no frozen criteria**. A thin desktop shell over the Hub web and a local Hub child process: solo login without token or SSO, quick task start, stage timeline with agent logs, working-copy diff with reviewer findings and visual QA, each with a TUI counterpart. Decisions taken 2026-11-14: Tauri shell, GitHub releases, separate app plus `keryx hub solo`, web first, template clarifying form. Acceptance criteria wait for operator review before freeze.
 >
 > - **0.29.31**: [Keryx Review V3](keryx-revview-v3/README.md) — **spec ready, D1–D7 accepted; runtime not implemented**. Schema v2/v1 compatibility, shared Keryx controller, native plus Keryx external general in first release, review-only authority, behavior-based coverage and initial large-review limits accepted. Implementation explicitly not started.
 >
 > - **0.29.30**: [Keryx Review V3](keryx-revview-v3/README.md) — **draft, runtime not implemented**. Preparation and coverage planning, catalog-backed generals/soldiers, shared tree limits and authority, native/external execution across harnesses.
 >
 > - **0.29.29**: [Unified model routing](keryx-unified-model-routing/README.md) — **spec ready, runtime v2 not implemented**. Four absolute model classes, cross-provider pools, one resolver, explicit fallback and reversible migration from category/tier mechanisms.

